Third-party components
----------------------

1. YADE (Yet Another Dynamic Engine) -- https://yade-dem.org

   postSPI is a set of user scripts executed inside YADE. The contact models,
   geometry functors and law functors it reads come from YADE. YADE is free
   software distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
   later; its copyright notices (kept in the individual files of the YADE
   tree) and its licence apply to it unchanged.

   Reference: Smilauer V., Chareyre B. (2021) Yade Documentation, 3rd edition,
   The Yade Project.

2. myYade -- https://github.com/PolyU-GUO/myYade

   The capillary (fCap) contact force used by the *_cap scripts
   (get_pressureMatrixZone5_cap.py / draw_pressureMatrixZone5_cap.py) is
   provided by the capillary model added on top of the YADE tree in the
   myYade fork (CapillaryCohPhys and Law2_ScGeom6D_CapillaryCohPhys_Capillarity).
   That component is Copyright (C) 2026 by Chang GUO and distributed under the
   GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

   Because postSPI depends on (and is only usable together with) these
   GPL-licensed components, postSPI itself is released under the same licence:
   GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.


